explanation:
Correct option:

{
   "Version":"2012-10-17",
   "Statement":[
      {
         "Effect":"Allow",
         "Action":[
            "s3:ListBucket"
         ],
         "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket"
      },
      {
         "Effect":"Allow",
         "Action":[
            "s3:GetObject"
         ],
         "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*"
      }
   ]
}
You manage access in AWS by creating policies and attaching them to IAM identities (users, groups of users, or roles) or AWS resources. A policy is an object in AWS that, when associated with an identity or resource, defines their permissions. AWS evaluates these policies when an IAM principal (user or role) makes a request. Permissions in the policies determine whether the request is allowed or denied. Most policies are stored in AWS as JSON documents. AWS supports six types of policies: identity-based policies, resource-based policies, permissions boundaries, service control policy (SCP)of AWS Organizations, access control list (ACL), and session policies.

s3:ListBucket is applied to buckets, so the ARN is in the form "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket", without a trailing / s3:GetObject is applied to objects within the bucket, so the ARN is in the form "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*", with a trailing /* to indicate all objects within the bucket mybucket

Therefore, this is the correct option.

Incorrect options:

{
   "Version":"2012-10-17",
   "Statement":[
      {
         "Effect":"Allow",
         "Action":[
            "s3:ListBucket",
            "s3:GetObject"
         ],
         "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket"
      }
   ]
}
This option is incorrect as it provides read-only access only to the bucket, not its contents.

{
   "Version":"2012-10-17",
   "Statement":[
      {
         "Effect":"Allow",
         "Action":[
            "s3:ListBucket",
            "s3:GetObject"
         ],
         "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*"
      }
   ]
}
This option is incorrect as it provides read-only access only to the objects within the bucket and it does not provide listBucket permissions to the bucket itself.

{
   "Version":"2012-10-17",
   "Statement":[
      {
         "Effect":"Allow",
         "Action":[
            "s3:ListBucket"
         ],
         "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*"
      },
      {
         "Effect":"Allow",
         "Action":[
            "s3:GetObject"
         ],
         "Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket"
      }
   ]
}
This option is incorrect as it provides listing access only to the bucket contents.

References:

https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/security/writing-iam-policies-how-to-grant-access-to-an-amazon-s3-bucket/

https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies.html

==================== GIẢI THÍCH TIẾNG VIỆT THEO FORMAT ====================

Đáp án đúng: A. Policy cần tách đúng bucket ARN và object ARN:
`{
  "Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement":[
    {"Effect":"Allow","Action":["s3:ListBucket"],"Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket"},
    {"Effect":"Allow","Action":["s3:GetObject"],"Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*"}
  ]
}`

Yêu cầu: Cho phép read-only cả bucket `mybucket` và nội dung object bên trong.

Giải thích: `s3:ListBucket` là bucket-level action nên Resource phải là `arn:aws:s3:::mybucket`, không có `/*`. `s3:GetObject` là object-level action nên Resource phải là `arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*`, đại diện cho tất cả object trong bucket. Có cả hai statement thì principal vừa list được bucket vừa đọc được object, nhưng không được Put/Delete.

Vì sao các đáp án khác không đúng: Policy có `s3:GetObject` nhưng dùng bucket ARN không có `/*` sẽ không cấp quyền đọc object. Policy dùng `arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*` cho `s3:ListBucket` lại áp dụng sai cấp resource. Gộp cả hai action vào bucket ARN hoặc object ARN đều khiến một action không match resource type cần thiết.

Mẹo thi: S3 bucket action → `arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name`; S3 object action → `arn:aws:s3:::bucket-name/*`. Đây là lỗi ARN rất hay xuất hiện trong đề IAM.

Tham khảo: https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/security/writing-iam-policies-how-to-grant-access-to-an-amazon-s3-bucket/
https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies.html

